course: dictionary
lesson: 10577
title: Undecided and still open
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You can often work out a word from its parts. Un- often means not, and decided means having made up your mind. So undecided means not yet having made up your mind. «I'm undecided about which club to join.» The speaker has not chosen yet, and the word about tells you what the choice is.
explain: Undecided can also describe things, not only people. «The date of the trip is still undecided.» Nothing is wrong with the trip; the day just has not been fixed yet. The word still is a clue: it tells you the decision is waiting, not finished.
explain: Context helps you check your meaning. Try it in the sentence: «I'm not yet sure which club to join» fits the first example, so your meaning is right. Being undecided is normal too: «Children cannot vote yet, and being undecided is fine.»
fact: Undecided means not yet having made up your mind.
fact: Undecided can also mean not yet settled or fixed, as in «The date of the trip is still undecided».
fact: An undecided game or match has not been won yet.
fact: In votes and surveys, undecided people have not chosen yet.
fact: Useful phrases: «still undecided», «undecided voters», «undecided about».
exercise: «I'm undecided about which club to join.» What does undecided mean here? | Already a member of every club | Sure, and joining the club today | *Not yet sure which club to pick | Angry with every club
exercise: «The date of the trip is still undecided.» What does undecided mean in this sentence? | Very early in the morning | Cancelled for ever | *Not yet fixed | Printed on the ticket
exercise: A class vote has many undecided pupils. What does this mean? | Pupils who have already voted twice | *Pupils who have not chosen yet | Pupils who never vote | Pupils who are ill today
test: What does undecided mean? | Having made up your mind for good | *Not yet having made up your mind | Very tired and sleepy | Lost on the way home
test: «The game is undecided with ten minutes left.» What does this tell you? | The game was won by the home team | The game is over | *The game has not been won yet | The game has been cancelled
exam: Which sentence shows someone who is undecided? | I bought two bags and I love them both. | I threw my bag away at the bus stop. | I have definitely chosen the blue bag. | *I still can't choose between the blue bag and the red bag.
